course: dictionary
lesson: 8247
title: A word from the animal world
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A rhinoceros is a very large, thick-skinned grey animal from Africa or Asia, with one or two horns on its nose. Its short, informal name is rhino.
explain: Context helps you see what a word means. In Rudyard Kipling's «Just So Stories» (1902), the story tells how animals «got» their shapes, and it says the Rhinoceros got «his folds». Folds are creases in the skin, and the story is explaining where they came from.
explain: Be careful: a rhinoceros beetle is a different creature. It is named after its horn, but it is an insect, not a rhino. When a word has more than one meaning, the sentence tells you which one the writer means.
fact: A rhinoceros is a large animal with thick skin, and it eats plants.
fact: There are five kinds of rhino: white and black rhinos in Africa, and Indian, Javan and Sumatran rhinos in Asia.
fact: Several rhinos are critically endangered because poachers kill them for their horns.
fact: A rhino's horn is made of keratin, the same material as our fingernails.
fact: «The woolly rhinoceros had thick fur and a flat front horn up to a metre long.»
exercise: Where is a rhinoceros's horn? | On its back | *On its nose | In its ears | On its tail
exercise: In Kipling's story, what does the Rhinoceros get? | His hump | His spots | *His folds | His long legs
exercise: Several rhinos are «critically endangered». What does that mean? | They can fly over long distances | They have lots of babies every year | *Very few are left and they could die out | They are very hungry all the time
test: «The woolly rhinoceros had thick fur and a flat front horn up to a metre long.» How long could that horn be? | Up to one kilometre | Up to one hundred metres | *Up to one metre | Up to ten centimetres
test: What is a rhino's horn made of, like our fingernails? | Feathers | *Keratin | Bone | Metal
exam: Which is the best meaning of rhinoceros? | A sea that lies between Africa and Arabia | A kind of tall tree with umbrella-shaped leaves | A small insect that lifts heavy things | *A very large, thick-skinned grey animal from Africa or Asia with one or two horns on its nose
